    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iuh1cda"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Negative inverted starting words like 'No sooner' must take 'than', whereas 'Hardly' and 'Scarcely' must take 'when' or 'before'.",
        "Do not use 'not' inside clauses introduced by 'Unless', 'Until', or 'Lest', as these conjunctions already carry a negative meaning.",
        "When subjects are joined by 'Either...or', 'Neither...nor', or 'Not only...but also', the verb agrees in person and number with the nearest subject.",
        "Never confuse 'Because' (shows cause/reason) with 'Prepositions' like 'Because of' (followed by a noun phrase rather than a clause)."
      ],
      "id": "mfp5qtg"
    },
